Patchsu patch 1 of 2: online restrictions (made against osu! commit 8cb6e6e68d). Only cuts online access; nothing else.

- Only read-only requests reach osu! servers (allow-list inside APIRequest): logging in, beatmaps (lookup / search / download),
  beatmap tags, leaderboards, player profiles and replay downloads. Everything else fails before touching the network.
- No score submission, no chat / notifications / spectator / multiplayer / presence connections, no crash reports,
  no update checks, no account creation.
- Menus: news, changelog, wiki, rankings, chat and social buttons and multiplayer / playlists / daily challenge are removed.

Applies and builds on its own. Apply 0002 on top for local profiles.

Also holds the empty Settings → "Patchsu" tab (LocalPriority/PatchSettings.cs: LocalPrioritySection + PatchSettingsSubsection),
so any patch can add its "Patch N. …" subsection without needing 0002. The tab only shows when an applied patch has one.

Also gives osu!'s last Fun mod (Bloom) a trailing comma in OsuRuleset.GetModsFor, so the mod patches (0500, 0501, 0502)
can each add their mods at the end of the list without conflicting with each other.

Also holds every patch's settings: LocalPriority/PatchsuSettings.cs keeps them in <osu! data>/patchsu-osu/PatchsuSettings.json,
one section per patch, only values that differ from their defaults (PatchsuSettings.Current.GetBindable / BindWith / Get / Set).
It's loaded in OsuGameBase.SetHost before game.ini, and flushed when the game closes. On the first start it renames the old
"osu-local" folder to "patchsu-osu" and keeps game.ini's old lines, so patches can take over settings that used to be there.

